# Cloudflare Pages header profile for the app's own origin.
#
# `public/` is dx's static directory (`[application] public_dir`, default
# "public"): a release `dx build --platform web` copies it verbatim into the
# emitted `public/`, so this file ships next to index.html and assets/ and the
# host applies it. It is NOT the landing's file and NOT the landing's headers —
# the two are separate origins (see docs/device-testing.md).
#
# Not verified live: nothing is deployed to this origin yet, and the landing's
# `/*` rules currently answer there because the app origin has no profile of its
# own. The three headers below that would stop the app are why this file exists:
#   * script-src needs 'wasm-unsafe-eval' — without it Chrome and Firefox refuse
#     to compile the module;
#   * connect-src needs wss: — a WebSocket is governed by connect-src, and
#     without it Veilid gets no network;
#   * camera must be allowed — `camera=()` somewhere up the chain kills the
#     browser QR scanner.
# COEP/COOP isolation: ON once the gpui threaded wasm build ships (the
# `gpui_ce_web` multithreaded feature links shared-memory and needs
# SharedArrayBuffer). The two headers below are sent unconditionally; the
# single-threaded fallback build tolerates them (it only *needs* isolation
# when linked for shared memory).

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), serial=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self' wss:; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
